&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div></description></item><item><title>03 Loops</title><link>https://blogs.timerring.com/posts/java-03-loops/</link><pubDate>Fri, 05 Jan 2024 22:07:53 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://blogs.timerring.com/posts/java-03-loops/</guid><description>&lt;p>Use &lt;code>==&lt;/code> to compare primitive data types for equality; for other types (such as strings and functions), use equals to compare them.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>02 Conditional Statements</title><link>https://blogs.timerring.com/posts/java-02-conditional-statements/</link><pubDate>Thu, 04 Jan 2024 19:42:08 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://blogs.timerring.com/posts/java-02-conditional-statements/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="if-statements">
